d235 4
a238 4
COMMENT  follows it in computing pixel coordinates from pixel coordinates (not
COMMENT  offsets).  However, the independent variables of the SIP polynomial
COMMENT  are offsets from the reference pixel.  This is handled here by setting
COMMENT  the renormalization parameters:
d244 2
a245 18
COMMENT  Likewise, the values computed by the SIP polynomial are corrections
COMMENT  to the pixel offsets.  Adding 1 to SIP polynomial coefficients,
COMMENT    DP1B.TPD.FWD.1 = 1 +  A_1_0,
COMMENT    DP1B.TPD.REV.1 = 1 + AP_1_0,
COMMENT    DP2B.TPD.FWD.2 = 1 +  B_0_1,
COMMENT    DP2B.TPD.REV.2 = 1 + BP_0_1,
COMMENT  converts the corrections into pixel offsets (where A_1_0 = B_0_1 = 0
COMMENT  normally for a SIP-conformant polynomial), and introducing the
COMMENT  constant terms of the polynomial,
COMMENT    DP1B.TPD.FWD.0 = CRPIX1,
COMMENT    DP1B.TPD.REV.0 = CRPIX1,
COMMENT    DP2B.TPD.FWD.0 = CRPIX2,
COMMENT    DP2B.TPD.REV.0 = CRPIX2,
COMMENT  converts the offsets into pixel coordinates.
COMMENT
COMMENT  These are the transformations done internally by WCSLIB (by sipset())
COMMENT  in implementing SIP as TPD.  The keycomments show the mapping between
COMMENT  SIP keywords and TPD coefficient indices.
d269 2
a270 2
DP1B    = 'TPD.FWD.0:              -3925.16' / TPD coefficient: 1
DP1B    = 'TPD.FWD.1:                   1.0' / TPD coefficient: x   1+A_1_0
d285 2
a286 2
DP1B    = 'TPD.REV.0:              -3925.16' / TPD coefficient: 1
DP1B    = 'TPD.REV.1:   1.00000596496231342' / TPD coefficient: x   1+AP_1_0
d305 2
a306 2
DP2B    = 'TPD.FWD.0:               4360.23' / TPD coefficient: 1
DP2B    = 'TPD.FWD.2:                   1.0' / TPD coefficient: y   1+B_0_1
d321 1
a321 1
DP2B    = 'TPD.REV.0:               4360.23' / TPD coefficient: 1
d323 1
a323 1
DP2B    = 'TPD.REV.2:   0.99999464658200091' / TPD coefficient: y   1+BP_0_1
d366 2
a367 2
DP1C    = 'TERM.1.COEFF:              -3925.16' / Poly coefficient: 1
DP1C    = 'TERM.2.COEFF:                     1' / Poly coefficient: x   1+A_1_0
d406 2
a407 2
DP2C    = 'TERM.1.COEFF:               4360.23' / Poly coefficient: 1
